TraceRAG
========

This project is an original implementation written from scratch.

Conceptual inspiration
----------------------

The idea of replacing a similarity-based vector index with a hierarchical
document tree that an LLM navigates by reasoning was popularised by
PageIndex (https://github.com/VectifyAI/PageIndex), released under the MIT
License, Copyright (c) 2025 Vectify AI.

TraceRAG re-implements that idea with a different architecture and a
different feature set. It does not contain source code copied from
PageIndex or from any other project. The upstream project is credited here
and in the README because crediting inspiration is the honest thing to do,
not because it is legally required for an independent re-implementation.

What is original to TraceRAG
----------------------------

1. An auditable retrieval trace: every candidate node visited during a
   query is recorded with its score, its scorer and the reason it was kept
   or pruned, and the trace is returned with the answer.
2. A per-sentence evidence ledger: each sentence of the generated answer is
   checked against the text of the nodes it cites, and sentences without
   support are flagged instead of being silently trusted.
3. Hybrid routing: a pure-Python BM25 router narrows each tree level before
   any model call, so the system degrades to a fully offline deterministic
   retriever when no API key is configured.
4. A built-in evaluation harness that scores the tree walker against a
   naive fixed-window chunking baseline on the same corpus.
5. Token and cost accounting per query.

